    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Five Card Stud rose to prominence during the American Civil War, evolving from earlier forms of Poker as a way to provide more information and betting opportunities per hand. It was the standard casino Poker variant for decades before being largely supplanted by Seven Card Stud in the mid-20th century.',
      originCountries: [
        'USA',
      ],
      timeline: [
        '1860s: First recorded play during the American Civil War.',
        '1910s: Becomes a staple of gambling houses in the United States and Europe.',
        "1965: Famously featured as the high-stakes game in the film 'The Cincinnati Kid'.",
        'Present: A rare but respected game in high-stakes card rooms and professional Mixed Game rotations.',
      ],
      evolution: "The game's transition from 5 cards to 7 cards (Seven Card Stud) allowed for more 'improvement' and complexity, which eventually pushed the 5-card version out of mainstream tournament play.",
